{
  "name": "Weekly HERE Tile Usage Check",
  "description": "One-time Friday Sep 11, 9pm Edmonton \u2014 checks the full week's HERE map tile usage from GoogleAPILog (Mon-Fri, with Monday footnoted as a testing day) and reports to the owner whether the tile cache fix has reduced daily API calls vs the ~2,900/day baseline.",
  "trigger": {
    "condition": null,
    "config": {
      "trigger_type": "scheduled",
      "events": [],
      "schedule_mode": "one_time",
      "cron_expression": null,
      "one_time_date": "2026-09-12T03:00:00Z",
      "timezone": "UTC",
      "interval_value": null,
      "interval_unit": null,
      "interval_anchor": null,
      "ends_type": "never",
      "ends_on_date": null,
      "ends_after_count": null
    }
  },
  "definition": {
    "do": [
      {
        "check_tile_usage": {
          "call": "invoke_superagent_step",
          "then": "end",
          "with": {
            "message": "End-of-week HERE tile usage check (agreed with owner Sep 7, 2026).\n\n1. Read the RxDeliver app (id 68570f3cd01bfa2d2408a9d6) GoogleAPILog entity records for api_type 'Map Tiles (HERE)' covering Mon Sep 7 through Fri Sep 11, 2026 (full days). Paginate with read_entities (limit 500, skip) until done; sum metadata.call_count per day and total.\n2. Monday Sep 7 was a heavy testing day (cache debugging) \u2014 exclude or footnote it when evaluating the trend; Tue-Fri are the clean signal.\n3. Compare with the pre-fix baseline (~2,900 tiles/day in Aug, e.g. 82,489 for the month).\n4. If daily counts are dropping substantially below baseline (cache working as expected), send the owner a short WhatsApp summary (brief \u2014 owner uses text-to-speech) saying the week's total, the average/day for Tue-Fri, and the % drop vs baseline.\n5. If counts are NOT dropping (still near baseline every day), investigate before messaging: check whether the counts are genuinely new tiles (new areas/zoom levels) or a cache regression (same tiles repeatedly), then report findings either way.\nNote: fresh log rows with real counts are often NEW tiles at unviewed zoom/location \u2014 check zoom levels/patterns before diagnosing a cache bug. Day boundaries: the app logs in UTC but the owner is in America/Edmonton \u2014 note that HERE's UTC-midnight reset can shift a few tiles across day boundaries."
          }
        }
      }
    ],
    "document": {
      "dsl": "1.0.0",
      "name": "here_tile_usage_weekly_check",
      "namespace": "base44",
      "version": "1.1"
    }
  }
}